# Project Overview

## Purpose

The Enterprise SOC & Detection Engineering Lab was designed to simulate the deployment and operation of an enterprise Windows environment monitored by a centralized Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) platform.

The project demonstrates practical skills used by Security Operations Center (SOC) analysts, detection engineers, and blue team defenders.

## Goals

- Deploy Active Directory
- Configure enterprise Windows endpoints
- Centralize Windows logging
- Implement Sysmon
- Develop Splunk detections
- Perform threat hunting
- Conduct vulnerability assessments
- Execute an incident response investigation

## Environment

- VMware Workstation Pro
- Windows Server 2022
- Windows 11 Enterprise
- Splunk Enterprise
- Sysmon
- Active Directory
- Group Policy

## Outcome

A fully documented enterprise security lab demonstrating SOC operations, detection engineering, vulnerability management, and incident response.

